   "tipo": "explicacion",
   "titulo": "Talk about what you like",
   "texto": [
    "After the match («gustar»), å + infinitive is used to say what you like to do: Jeg liker å lese («I like to read»). In Spanish the infinitive goes without a word equivalent to å.",
    "In Norwegian can also be invited with Vil du bli med? («You want to come with me?»). Bli med is a fixed expression."
